# Beads repo overrides

This rule takes precedence over the bd-generated `beads.mdc` rule, which `bd setup`
may rewrite. It is a separate file so those rewrites cannot drop it.

- Durable work items go in `bd` (see AGENTS.md). In-session scratch todos
  (TodoWrite, TaskCreate, or similar) and agent memory features remain allowed
  for private scratch use; they are not shared project state, and anything
  durable belongs in a ticket.
- Never run a bare `bd dolt push`. Publishing ticket data is done only with
  `scripts/bd-push.sh`, and only when the task or owner explicitly authorises
  it. Every push publishes the whole tracker and its Dolt history to a public
  remote, so never write internal ids, emails, phone numbers or secrets into a
  ticket, even temporarily. Never force-push or replace `refs/dolt/data`.
- Do not use `bd provenance record` in this repo; provenance uses the labels and
  audit log described in AGENTS.md.
